id: ops-3j1z
title: "Repair an incomplete release triple, instead of only reporting it every day"
description: "The release-completeness audit now runs unconditionally after Create GitHub release, so an incomplete predecessor is reported every day until it is repaired. Nothing repairs it. A run that publishes to npm and pushes its tag and then fails before creating the GitHub Release leaves a triple that no subsequent run completes, because the next run has no source changes and skips the release path entirely. That is exactly what happened here: v2026.08.28, v2026.08.29 and v2026.08.31 were published and tagged with no GitHub Release for fourteen days, and the three releases were created by hand on 2026-08-31, each body generated from its committed changelog section. The automation should do the same: for every release tag that has a published npm version and no GitHub Release, create the release from that version's changelog section. Held out of pull request 77 deliberately, because it is a write path into the releases API inside a job that already publishes to npm and pushes tags, and it deserves its own review rather than arriving inside a change about detection. Raised in review by Greptile as P1 and by CodeRabbit as a Major data-integrity finding."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-31T12:41:05.904Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-11T05:54:25.544Z"
author: claude-orchestrator
acceptance_criteria: "For each release tag with a published npm version and no GitHub Release, the release job creates the missing GitHub Release from that version's committed changelog section; the step is idempotent, so a run with nothing to repair makes no API writes; a tag with no published npm version is never given a GitHub Release, since that would assert a release that was never published; the repair is covered by hermetic tests with an injected client and no network"
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  ops-i8yp,blocked_by,"2026-08-31T12:41:06.966Z",claude-orchestrator,"cli:update:dep",detected
comments[16]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T21:42:08.963Z",codex-sol,"Baseline acceptance: built package and compiled completeness verifier exercised with a real SDK-created scratch pm tracker and local git release tag v2026.08.28. Recorded npm inventory contains 2026.8.28 and GitHub has no release. Two successive audits both report the same missing GitHub Release and perform zero repairs. Plan: explicit --repair flag, verified npm provenance naming gitHead and repository, committed manifest/changelog checks, preflight all candidates before writes, conditional tag creation and idempotent release creation; never publish. Tests use recorded verification output, injected process boundary and local git repositories."
  "2026-10-07T21:47:24.750Z",codex-sol,"Implemented conservative preflight and conditional repair adapter, including verified npm signature-audit bundles rather than trusting dist.attestations presence. Daily workflow explicitly passes --repair after the current release; default invocation remains report-only. Recovery checks all incomplete candidates before writes and uses only immutable committed changelog sections. Repeated and concurrent recovery is exercised with local git remotes and real SDK-created trackers. npm signature audit is the cryptographic verification boundary; tests inject recorded command responses and never call write APIs."
  "2026-10-07T21:49:17.016Z",codex-sol,"Read-only recording from npm 11.17.0 for published pm-ops 2026.8.28 captured real verified bundles and caught the actual attestationBundles array shape. Added offline regression fixture. Historical registry gitHead differs from the signed source commit, so repair correctly refuses this coordinate instead of treating a valid signature as evidence of the release commit. This is covered by existing owner items ops-xf9a and ops-uizs; no duplicate or upstream issue filed."
  "2026-10-07T21:54:11.123Z",codex-sol,"Revert proof: behaviorally replaced only repairReleaseCompleteness with the former report-only audit and rebuilt successfully. The three key scenarios (missing release, npm-only orphan and built-package orphan beside a real tracker) all loaded and failed assertions: 0 passed, 3 failed, zero skips. Restored the function and rebuilt successfully. Focused coverage verifies the new module and audit wrapper at the unchanged 100 percent thresholds; full release gates are next. Existing optional fleet-data tests remain unconfigured to respect this task scope."
  "2026-10-07T21:57:36.225Z",codex-sol,"Linked acceptance receipt: pm test ops-3j1z --run --progress passed all 53 focused tests in a workspace snapshot using pm_context_mode=none and real scratch trackers; zero failures or skips. This pm configuration disables automatic test-result tracking, so this comment preserves the result. No SDK defect found. Both full release commands remain required; test thresholds and optional real-fleet scope are unchanged."
  "2026-10-07T22:10:59.414Z",codex-sol,"First Bun release gate failed only in the existing installed pm CLI --repos routing acceptance: packed pm package install exceeded the unchanged 30-second child timeout. Suite result: 485 passed, 1 failed, 2 optional fleet-data skips; all repair scenarios passed and aggregate coverage was 100 percent in all four dimensions. The npm gate passed 486 tests with 2 optional skips. Investigating with an isolated installer retry before rerunning the complete Bun gate; no threshold or timeout weakened."
  "2026-10-07T22:14:36.397Z",codex-sol,"Installer retry passed the exact existing packed --repos routing test in isolation: 1 passed, zero failures/skips, unchanged child timeouts. Now rerunning the complete bun run release:check with no code, threshold or timeout changes. Timing evidence remains linked to ops-gp0d."
  "2026-10-07T22:20:14.936Z",codex-sol,"Final receipts: npm run release:check passed; bun run release:check passed on the unchanged retry. Each full gate ran 488 tests: 486 passed, zero failed, 2 pre-existing optional real-fleet skips. All 25 authored source files were reported at 100 percent statements, lines, branches and functions; duplication remained 0 percent, 223 documented declarations passed, production audit had zero vulnerabilities, and pack/changelog/attestation/lifecycle gates passed. Both pack checks produced the same artifact shasum 3b5f27a8ba3466cf711b538734295a7a1c61fced. Revert proof: three behavior assertions failed with only the repair function reverted and a successful rebuild; restored focused suite passed 53/53 via pm test snapshot. README and fixtures document provenance drift refusal and immutable-ref concurrency limits. No pm SDK bug found; automatic test-result tracking is disabled, so comments preserve receipts. Claim released for orchestrator review; item intentionally not closed."
  "2026-10-07T22:38:43.982Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeQL review (PR #150): heading parsing used /\\s+-\\s+/ (polynomial backtracking; 50,000 spaces took ~4.8s) and is now linear (/\\s-\\s/ search); remoteTag validates the release tag at the call site so only release coordinates reach git argv (the argument was always refs/tags/<tag>, so not option-injectable, but the guard is now local and explicit). Two new tests fail against the previous code."
  "2026-10-10T02:50:31.421Z",codex-sol,"Independent read-only assessment of PR #150 at 0a04adfa2e507339ab90e0f0bf6a75b177c7173b: npm audit signatures is a real verification boundary, source/commit checks and preflight no-write behavior are sensible. Injected verified-audit fixtures show evidenceFromAudit accepts absent externalParameters.workflow and an unapproved workflow path/ref. This is parser-contract evidence, not a live signature bypass; source authorization requirements need explicit review. No branch modification or release write performed. CodeRabbit final-head review reports no actionable comments; Greptile only trial-ended bodies, Sourcery quota plus guide, Cubic neutral and no Gemini/Copilot receipts. CodeQL command-injection comments are option-shaped false positives mitigated by release-tag validation; prior regex finding was fixed and regression tested. Green CI is not complete review approval. Companion: pm-cli-website-session-2026-10-10."
  "2026-10-11T05:00:43.513Z",codex-agent,Merged origin/main into the reviewed feature branch without rebasing. No unmerged textual conflicts; field-aware drivers united comments/docs and reanchored both history streams. Reconciliation dry-run preserved both main-side events and reported zero reverted fields. Keeping repair guards and main publisher scanning/artifact-time Git-config behavior intact. Main records an unresolved workflow authorization parser contract; this maintenance pass preserves that review risk.
  "2026-10-11T05:02:31.549Z",codex-agent,"Post-merge revert proof: replaced only repairReleaseCompleteness with report-only inventory audit; npm run build passed. The missing-release, npm-only-orphan and built-package acceptance cases loaded and failed assertions: 3 tests, 0 passed, 3 failed, 0 skipped, 0 canceled, 0 TODO. Restored the exact function and rebuilt successfully. npm ci completed with 5 high findings in the full dependency inventory; npm audit --omit=dev --ignore-scripts --json reports zero production vulnerabilities. Files link syntax accepts one CSV entry per --add; corrected an initial multi-argument invocation. Linked duplicate command was removed and the original snapshot/none context preserved."
  "2026-10-11T05:13:16.229Z",codex-agent,"The first post-merge linked acceptance run reached its existing 180-second timeout after five passing repair scenarios, with no assertion failures reported before SIGTERM. Automatic linked-result recording remains disabled by project policy. The first npm gate reports a failure in the existing real-c8 fixture while the remaining SDK-backed cases continue; complete counts and a focused unchanged retry are pending. Full-audit findings match the development-only braces/jscpd dependency chain already owned by ops-braces-audit, so no duplicate follow-up was created. Main and reviewed feature source files compare exactly to their respective source commits; all thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-11T05:20:47.833Z",codex-agent,"Unchanged linked acceptance retry with an isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration passed: pm test ops-3j1z --run --progress executed 55 tests, 55 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped/canceled/TODO, elapsed about 95 seconds under the original 180-second timeout. The first npm run release:check completed 597 tests: 512 passed, 83 failed, 2 optional fleet-data skips, 0 canceled/TODO. Failures include a 30-second c8 child timeout, an operations setup conflicting-merge child timeout, and the isolated parser runtime budget; coverage correctly failed afterward. Bun and the required isolated-HOME npm gates are running sequentially with unchanged thresholds and test timeouts."
  "2026-10-11T05:46:35.924Z",codex-agent,"Required full gate receipts: the normal npm run release:check failed with 597 tests, 512 passed, 83 failed, 2 optional fleet-data skips; Bun and the required isolated-HOME npm run each failed with 597 tests, 594 passed, 1 failed, 2 identical optional skips. All runs had 0 canceled/TODO. The latter two reported 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines across all 25 configured source files; their only failure was the unchanged 30-second pm package install child in the packed --repos acceptance. Coverage reports are invalidated on failed runs as designed. Linked isolated-HOME acceptance passed 55/55 with zero skips and the unchanged 180-second linked timeout. The function-only revert proof loaded and failed three assertions, then restoration/rebuild passed. The installer owner ops-gp0d is enriched; an unchanged focused retry and the verifiers skipped by the failed chain are running. Full release gates remain red; no approval or publication readiness is claimed."
  "2026-10-11T05:54:21.311Z",codex-agent,"Final maintenance receipt: the unchanged installed --repos acceptance passed in a focused retry (1/1, zero failures/skips/canceled/TODO; selected case about 110 seconds, total with setup about 292 seconds). This does not supersede the three failed full-gate receipts. The remainder of release:check passed independently: production audit zero vulnerabilities, dry-run pack 58 files with shasum e1f7fe3640f99ed4b1686bebe301987354cd3fe3, changelog consistency/date, 1 provenance-bearing publish invocation and all 8 canonical/installed lifecycle policies. Source comparisons preserve both reviewed repair behavior and main publisher/artifact-time behavior; dist rebuilt without differences. Trusted PM reconciliation preserved both main events with zero reverted fields, and new tracker/receipt content passed privacy checks. No new CLI defect was established; list-open is deprecated, initial context signals were rebuilt, and result recording is disabled by existing policy. Workflow authorization review, development audit owner ops-braces-audit and timing owner ops-gp0d remain open boundaries. Claim release and final scripted changelog regeneration follow; item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification. No push, PR merge, artifact release/tag, publication, upstream write or hosted change performed."
